mmunity, recognizing that the effects of gastrointestinal symptoms, including diarrhea and constipation, can differ greatly depending on socio-economic factors.", "WORLD HEALTH ORGANIZATION:The World Health Organization (WHO) is a specialized agency of the United Nations that is responsible for international public health. Its mandate includes the development of guidelines on various aspects of health, including nutrition. The WHO plays a crucial role in coordinating global health efforts and setting standards to improve health outcomes worldwide.", "CANCER SOCIETY:The American Cancer Society is an organization focused on cancer prevention and research, providing guidelines on nutrition and physical activity.", "RUEL MT:Ruel MT is a co-author of a study on dietary diversity and child nutritional status, focusing on nutrition and health surveys.", "FOOTE JA:Foote JA is an author of research on dietary variants and their impact on nutrient adequacy among adults.", "MURPHY SP:Murphy SP is a co-author of a study discussing dietary variants and their effects on nutrient adequacy.", "WANG X:Wang X is an author engaged in various research studies focusing on health outcomes related to dietary habits. This includes investigations into urinary excretion and its implications for health, as well as the relationship between fruit consumption and gastric cancer. Additionally, Wang X has contributed to a systematic review that examines the association between fruit and vegetable consumption and mortality rates. Through these studies, Wang X has made significant contributions to understanding the impact of diet on health.", "ECKEL RH:Eckel RH is a prominent researcher and co-author of the 2013 American Heart Association (AHA) and American College of Cardiology (ACC) guideline on lifestyle management aimed at reducing cardiovascular risk. In addition to being a co-author, Eckel RH also served as a contributor to this important guideline, which provides recommendations for lifestyle changes to help mitigate cardiovascular risk factors.", "BANTLE JP:Bantle JP is a notable researcher and co-author of the American Diabetes Association's position statement on nutrition recommendations for diabetes. He has made significant contributions to the field through his studies on the metabolic effects of dietary sucrose and fructose in diabetic subjects, enhancing the understanding of how these sugars impact individuals with diabetes.", "KUSHI LH:Kushi LH is a co-author of the American Cancer Society Guidelines on nutrition and physical activity for cancer prevention.", "SLAVIN JL:Slavin JL is an author discussing the health benefits of fruits and vegetables in nutrition research."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}